 "caveats": [
  "Both RHi columns reuse pyEPM plume output computed at RHi = 110%. Ambient RHi moves the ice number handed to APCEMM by at most 1.6% (scripts/diag_rhi_ice_sensitivity.py), so the comparison isolates the dispersion phase rather than the formation phase.",
  "APCEMM's ambient temperature is a systematic 0.164 K below the labelled T_amb: the pipeline's ISA constant is 223.314 K where the met generator's ISA gives 223.15 K at 10 km. A bias, not noise.",
  "A panel going dark means the contrail dissipated. A panel still bright at 20 h is right-censored -- APCEMM stopped, the contrail did not. 49% of the RHi 110% campaign is censored; per-case status distinguishes the two.",
  "Rasters are area-weighted means over ~276 x 11 m cells, against a native grid of 50 x 7 m. That conserves ice mass but dilutes peak IWC; the peak_iwc_kg_m3 scalar carries the undiluted native value.",
  "quantization.floor_kg_m3 is a storage floor, not the colour scale. It is set an order of magnitude below anything worth drawing because dilution at the contrail edge pushes cells under it irrecoverably. Clamp the colour scale at display_floor_kg_m3 instead.",
  "The encoded range 1e-10..6e-6 kg/m^3 is set so nothing clamps: the measured campaign maximum is 5.484e-6. A colour scale may saturate wherever it likes -- notebook_CoMET.ipynb uses 3e-6 -- but note that 3e-6 saturates a third of the frames that hold ice.",
  "The window is fixed for all times, so a young contrail (~10 m wide at t=0) occupies well under one cell. Early frames are faint by construction, not by failure."
 ],
